> Servings: 5

= Ingredients

@olive oil{3/8%cup}\
@salt{1%teaspoon}\
@ground cumin{5/8%teaspoon}\
@black pepper{5/8%teaspoon}\
@dried oregano, crumbled{3/8%teaspoon}\
@skinless boneless chicken breasts and/or thighs, cut into 2 1/2 -inch pieces{1 7/8%pounds}\
@red bell pepper, cut lengthwise into 1/2-inch-wide strips{1 1/4}\
@Italian frying or Cubanelle pepper, cut lengthwise into 1/2-inch-wide strips{1 1/4}\
@medium red onion, cut lengthwise into 1/2-inch-wide strips{1 1/4}\
@(8- to 10-ounce) container prepared hummus (preferably Sabra spicy or classic){1 1/4}\
@Accompaniment: toasted pita bread{}

= Directions
Preheat broiler.

Line a large shallow baking pan with foil.

Stir together oil, salt, cumin, pepper, and oregano in a large bowl, then toss with chicken and vegetables. Arrange in baking pan without crowding and broil 4 to 6 inches from heat, stirring once, until chicken is just cooked through and vegetables are lightly charred, about 8 minutes. Divide hummus among plates and top with chicken and vegetables.
